                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Posting for my wife, who played this on Family Share.\n\nPEG is a hidden little gem of a puzzle game! I loved it! Considering how much content this game has, I think its normal price of  $1 USD it is an absolute steal!\n\nThe gameplay is based on classic Peg Solitaire but with a twist - each board has two colors to clear instead of one. Jumping two pegs of the same color will remove a peg from the board, but jumping two pegs of different colors will not. This lead to a lot of fun puzzles where you have to use pegs of different colors as \"bridges\" to get around the board.\n\nFor such a small project, this game has an incredible amount of polish. The ambient soundscape is relaxing, the graphics have a cute paper cut-out style, and the game includes quality of life features such as a move undo button and a quick restart.\n\nIf you love solving Chess or Go problems, or just love abstract puzzle games in general, then I highly recommend this game!",
